      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Couldn't you already do this if the face tracking app supported OSC and sent the correct messages (and worked in the background)?\n\nJust find it very unlikely that VRChat would natively support face tracking on android, since they'd have to make their own face tracking software for it.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
    {
      "__v": 0,
      "_id": "64e0e6356f0515099870c573",
      "author": {
        "_id": "619ffdfe00e2a864e7efb2e1",
        "alias": "Cooing Porpoise",
        "aliasID": "65c28068ed6eefce4c52fc54",
        "anonymized": false,
        "avatarURL": "https://canny-assets.io/images/257f6ee16c9e88419904d2d6142c0f50.png",
        "created": "2021-11-25T21:19:58.176Z",
        "name": "Spiro Renard",
        "serviceAccount": false,
        "urlName": null
      },
      "authorID": null,
      "boardID": "6466ab9cd0071b0936f27dcd",
      "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
      "created": "2023-08-19T15:56:37.394Z",
      "deleted": false,
      "fileURLs": [],
      "files": [],
      "imageURLs": [],
      "integrationSourceType": null,
      "internal": false,
      "itemSourceType": null,
      "mentionedUserIDs": null,
      "mentionedUsers": [],
      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": "64e0e1d9883c5a9d1efee67c",
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "64e0d98d2ab2a3099f0ae937",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 1
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "While it's theoretically possible, there's a notable challenge when it comes to mobile implementation of OSC (Open Sound Control). The majority of mobile OSC applications aren't designed to seamlessly run in the background on your phone; their primary purpose is to remain actively open while you enjoy content on another device, such as your Quest.\n\nIt's improbable that VRChat would develop their own face tracking software for Android in this context. The requirement for native support for face tracking on Android would entail significant effort, including the development of proprietary face tracking software, which seems unlikely for VRChat to undertake.\n\nFor a relevant comparison, you can take a look at Roblox's implementation of face tracking in the following video: https://youtu.be/LJWBZtjgBgI?t=21 . This might provide some insight into how face tracking could potentially work in the context of mobile applications.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
    {
