      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{619ffdfe00e2a864e7efb2e1|full_name}: OSC wise I expect apps to appear to address those issues, just like we have a few FBT apps on phones nowadays.\n\nAnd to the later portions, I expected you to provide a counter-argument for how it could feasibly work, using Roblox as an example can work as a proof of concept, but they've got so many more resources than VRChat that it can only work as a rough proof of concept.\n\nSo I guess I will. There are a few open source face tracking programs, in theory VRChat could use one of those, however I find it unlikely that they would until after they start supporting face tracking and not just eye tracking.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
